<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claude Maxwell MacDonald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Claude MacDonald was a British soldier and diplomat who became commissioner and consul-general of the Oil Rivers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in 1891, setting up an administration at Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabar">Calabar</a>. The territory became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> Coast Protectorate in 1893. He was later British minister in Peking during the Boxer siege of the legations and ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claude-maxwell-macdonald.jpg" alt="Claude Maxwell MacDonald" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SirClaudeMacdonald.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1893 the Oil Rivers Protectorate was extended inland and renamed the Niger Coast Protectorate, under the commissioner and consul-general <b>Claude MacDonald</b>, with headquarters at Old Calabar.</blockquote><a href="/state/niger-coast-protectorate">Niger Coast Protectorate</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1887 consul Harry Johnston deported King Jaja of Opobo, and from 1891 <b>Claude MacDonald</b>, as commissioner and consul-general, set up a proper administration at Old Calabar with customs and courts.</blockquote><a href="/state/oil-rivers-protectorate">Oil Rivers Protectorate</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Gwalior, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=26.21,78.18&amp;year=1892" aria-label="Gwalior on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6614 1201 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Claude Maxwell MacDonald"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7064 1471h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=26.21,78.18&amp;year=1892">What was here in 1892? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
